> Team, data is retrieved from a Log Analytics workspace using log queries written in Kusto Query Language (KQL).

> Kusto Query Language (KQL) is the query language used in Azure Monitor, specifically for querying logs stored in Log Analytics workspaces.

> For example, type AzureActivity and click Run.

> Now team, here you can see the log in the result section. this is the data related to subscription activity.

> you can expant any of the log to see the data in details.

> Lets view a count of activity log records for each category, use the following query, so type- 

 AzureActivity
| summarize count() by CategoryValue

and click on run- now you can see the count of the categories.

> Now, lets retrieve all records in the administrative category, so type- 

AzureActivity
| where CategoryValue == "Administrative"

> Here, you can see all the records related to the Administrative category.

> Note: Team, if you're not familiar with KQL (Kusto Query Language), you can refer to the KQL documentation available online for help.

Note: There is no data ingestion charges for activity logs. Retention charges for activity logs are only applied to the period extended past.
the default retention period of 90 days. You can increase the retention period to up to 12 years.

