Now, team, let’s see how to create an alert for the activity log.

Go back to the Log Analytics workspace.

Run the following query: AzureActivity

Click on the three dots on the top right corner, then select New alert rule.

Signal name is already selected as Custom log query,
because we are using a custom query.

Leave the value as default:

Measure type: Table rows

Aggregation type: Count

Aggregation granularity: 5 minutes

Scroll down and here:

Operator: Greater than

Threshold value: 10 (This means we will get an alert whenever the count of rows is greater than 10.)

Frequency of evaluation: 5 minutes (Means, we want this query to runs every 5 minutes.)

