> What does "Global Region" mean in Azure Monitor Action Group?

The "Global Region" refers to the global scope of certain Azure services that are not tied to a specific Azure region (like East US, West Europe, etc.).

> In the context of Action Groups, "Global Region" means:

The action group is not region-specific and can be used across all regions and resources in your Azure subscription/tenant.

> Why is this useful?

You can reuse the same action group (e.g., for email, SMS, webhook alerts) across different VMs or services located in different Azure regions.
It's managed centrally, and you don’t have to create multiple action groups for each region.

